00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:46.190
He's really good at line shots,
so diggers, look for that.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.480
When Aoki and Haijima are up front,
watch out for feints and dumps.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.810
Bamboo

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:54.980
Subaru!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:58.520
Are you going to see Dr. Toyama
again next Saturday?

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.480
Yes. It's just my usual checkup.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.440
Make sure you tell me how that checkup goes.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.770
I know.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:10.150
Subaru- <i>senpai</i> ! Wanna go play some
beach volleyball out on the beach?

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.520
If you've got that much energy left over,

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.810
I'll wake you up early tomorrow
so you can practice some more!

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.400
Let's go, Subaru- <i>senpai</i> !

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:24.270
Man, what's with this training camp? How lame.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:28.310
All right! Then let's have the first and
second years up against the third years!

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:27.970
H-Hey!

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.770
Bring it on!

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:32.980
Why are you encouraging this, Subaru?

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.150
The energy we've got today is for today.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.150
We'll make sure to practice in the morning, too!

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.850
Haijima, how are we going to stop Mimura?

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:52.650
If we give the Demon Bazooka any time to hit,

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.020
we're not going to be able to stop him.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:59.900
We need to make it hard for Mimura
to hit starting with our serves.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.190
When we can't do that, we should
concentrate on how to score

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:07.060
rather than avoid getting scored on.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:09.810
So you're saying blocking
is out of the question.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.520
Not entirely.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:15.020
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> is asking Haijima for advice.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.900
Haijima, can we leave it to you to
come up with a strategy against Mimura?

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.980
I've thought of at least three things.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.310
I'll incorporate them into our practice today.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.190
We're counting on you.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:24.850
Right.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.560
To think the weak little team
that kept losing in the first round

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.520
is going to make it to
the representative play-offs.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.940
We can finally challenge the Fukui champions.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:42.310
We should be proud of ourselves!

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.350
Let's go to the Spring Tournament!

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.440
Yeah!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.340
Episode 9: 'The Unbeaten and the Dark Horse'

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.770
Subaru...

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:58.440
Once your high school tournament is over,
want to consider having surgery again?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.900
Surgery?

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.520
On both?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.190
You're okay right now,

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.940
so I won't stop you from playing
at the Spring Tournament in January.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.310
But you're basically walking around
with timebombs in both knees.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:16.310
You're going to some major college
in the Kanto or Kansai region, right?

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:18.940
I do have some offers on the table...

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:24.810
Then you'll be able to see some
reputable doctors in Tokyo or Osaka.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:30.270
You might have to give up your first
or second years of college, but...

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.150
Two years?!

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:35.150
You're still in high school.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:38.900
You need to think about your upcoming career!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.480
I really don't want these opened up again.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.730
Not to mention, not being able
to play for two years...

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.940
I won't be able to bounce
back like I did before?

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.980
Oh, how rude of me.
I didn't see you. Have a seat.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.020
Thank you.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.060
No worries.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:10.940
Hey, you're Mimura, aren't you?
The volleyball player.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:12.150
Yes.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.980
I knew it. I wasn't entirely sure,

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.980
but I saw your tracksuit.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:19.650
Ah...

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.850
Keep doing your best out there.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.730
Thank you very much. I will.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.360
"Fukui High School
Newcomer Volleyball
Tournament Venue"

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.810
Hey, it's Mimura from Fukuho.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:34.730
He's so cool!

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.980
He's so tall!

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:38.600
Subaru- <i>senpai</i> ! Please take this.

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.850
Oh, thanks.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.560
What is this?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.350
I don't think I've seen it before. Is it new?

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.400
I bought it as soon as I saw it
at the convenience store yesterday!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:53.100
It's raspberry milk flavor! You like
berry-flavored things the best, right?

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.730
Wow, I'm surprised you know that.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:56.770
Subaru!

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.730
Over here!

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:01.560
You're late. The opening ceremonies are over.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.900
We're seeded. We don't have a match today.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.980
Why are you getting hit on?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:07.850
You can't have any.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:09.100
I don't want any!

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.980
So where's Ochi?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:15.060
He's back at HQ.
Coach asked him to do something.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.850
Subaru, doesn't look like
anyone from Seiin is here.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.310
Well, that's not surprising

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:23.980
since Oda's team doesn't have
that many first or second years.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:27.730
They'll probably just hold out
until the representative play-offs.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:31.650
Probably. Hey, Kohei.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.480
Don't mess up before we play our rivals.

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.940
If you don't win, you're not
gonna be in the play-offs.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.350
Got it! I'm gonna get all my line
shots through and win this thing!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:45.150
Is that so? Then if you lose any set,
there'll be punishment for you.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:48.770
Uh... Exactly what kind of punishment?

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.900
Let's see... What should it be?

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.400
We'll have you be a one-man cheer squad
for some girls after school.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.600
Wha-- N-No way!

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:00.100
I'd rather jump into the moat in front
of the prefectural office naked...

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.400
Then let's do that.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.100
Wait, uh... Okay, fine.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.230
I'll do it if all the other
second years have to do it, too.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:06.830
No way!

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:07.690
You're on your own!

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:12.150
Anyway... Let's go get Ochi and get outta here.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.350
You're not going to watch
the other schools play?

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:17.230
We just need to worry about
our team being in top shape.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.770
Hey, Ochi- <i>senpai</i> 's back.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.270
Subaru, how'd things go with Dr. Toyama?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.560
Hm? It was fine. No changes.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.310
I see...

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.900
I'm in perfect shape! Don't you worry!

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:45.190
I have to be until I take you to the
center court at the Spring Tournament.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.770
This is our last Spring Tournament.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:11:00.560
We'll make it to the center court at
the Spring Tournament with this team.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.270
We're counting on you, Ace.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.730
You got it!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.690
Next! The fourth rotation!

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.310
Kuroba! Your feet aren't moving!

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.060
Next, the fifth rotation!

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:46.150
Two attackers up front.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.810
Stop!

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:58.520
Haijima, you good?

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.850
Yes.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.520
We should probably wipe down
the floor. It's getting dangerous.

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:08.270
What? You guys out of energy
already? Talk about lame.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.980
You got a break!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.730
Buck up!

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:16.150
We need to perfect our team within
these three days at this training camp!

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.420
I can't hear you!

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:17.980
Right!

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:22.100
Ah, working hard, I see.

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:25.770
How about you pair up with
Hokao during this training, Oda.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.310
Y-Yes, sir.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:31.350
Kanno with Uchimura. Okuma with Kuroba.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.400
And then, Aoki with Haijima.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.520
Make sure you all get along
outside of practice, too.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.770
Right!

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:44.810
Now, then... Why don't we have a little
competition so you boys can get closer?

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:46.270
Let's have a serving competition.

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:49.190
Well, in that case, there should be a prize.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:53.650
I know. Let's say the winning pair
gets to order the other pairs around.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.690
That's not a prize! That's punishment!

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.600
Guess you're just going to have to win, then.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.980
At least this will keep us on our toes.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:05.770
Make sure you get along with your partners.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:13.690
Just one after another...

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.150
Seriously?

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.770
Three in a row...

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.400
Hey, hold up!

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.020
Is he gonna end it without letting
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> even serve once?!

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.940
Why the hell are you so competitive?!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:34.350
Haijima! Don't worry about me!
Just keep hitting those targets!

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:48.520
Wha--?! How'd you hit that with a jump floater?!

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.060
If you hit the ball just in the right spot,

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:54.190
you can somewhat control
how it's going to curve.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.850
And done! Looks like we're first place!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.560
Th-That's not fair...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.730
He knew what he was getting with Haijima...

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.400
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> is pretty calculating.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:08.270
Whoever's up next, do your best out there!

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.700
"1st place"

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.950
"2nd place"

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.790
"3rd place"

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.620
"Last place"

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.230
Okuma, you're gonna have to work on
hitting the ball where you aim first.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.520
And Kuroba, when you know where
you're gonna hit, don't hit at 100%.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.810
Try hitting at 70%.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:29.440
Once we're done today,
you two will be practicing serves.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.270
Right!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.980
So about your orders...

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:33.940
What?!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.600
Wait, that wasn't it?!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.650
Those were just orders from your captain.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.520
This isn't fair!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.600
This sucks.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:43.150
Your orders as last place
are to raise your ranks

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.600
on your finals on each subject at least 20%.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:50.770
Third place go up 10%, and 2nd place
go up 5%. If you can't pull this off,

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.100
punishment awaits.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:52.950
What?!

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.060
Wait, why?!

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:56.400
Wait, this is super harsh!

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.650
Students need to put their studies first.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:02.690
Even if we go to Tokyo in January,
our finals still await.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.940
I'm not saying anything impossible here.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:08.900
If you're placed at 100,
you just need to go up 20 ranks.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.940
Hang on, you!

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:16.310
Don't go sighing like that just
because you think you got out of this!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:19.690
You're in more trouble
than anyone with modern lit!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.650
This doesn't apply to me. I placed first.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.230
I'll do something about
Haijima's Japanese classes.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.100
Huh? I-I'm fine...

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:32.350
No, you're not! We're doing this.
Vice captain's orders.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:38.560
How'd the girls' newcomer match go?

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.480
I guess they lost in the second round.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.850
I see.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.600
I heard Fukuho kept winning.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.150
I guess they're pretty strong
even without their third years.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.730
Oh, yeah. I heard that Fukuho
had a training camp last week, too.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:57.520
I heard they had practice matches
all day with a college team.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:00.480
What's with those connections?

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.480
Fukuho's got some alum that
continue playing at the college level,

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.560
so they've got plenty of connections.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:10.350
No, I was talking about your intel, Aoki- <i>senpai</i> .

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:17.480
Aoki.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:22.270
For not playing any sports
in middle school, you're pretty built.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:25.980
You think so? I was a twig
when I was a first year.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.060
Then you must've practiced a lot.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:33.770
You don't need to mention that.
You're ruining my image.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.980
You don't need to compliment me.

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:39.940
But you don't seem to mind
letting me have my way.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.150
I'm sure you realize this more than anyone,

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:46.850
but if we fail to connect at the finals
like we did at the prelims, we're doomed.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.980
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.350
You don't need to thank me.

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:53.690
You're not the only one who wants to win.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:58.770
I can't say that I like that our coach
sees through all of us, but...

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:04.100
I'm not going to continue
playing volleyball after I graduate.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.230
What?!

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:09.980
Was it that surprising?
This is just a club for me.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:13.980
But I did enjoy my three years doing it.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:18.560
I never thought being tall was a good thing.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.400
But when I started playing volleyball,

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:23.810
I finally thought there was
something good about being tall.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:27.560
I'm grateful that Oda invited me to play.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.730
Oda invited you?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:32.060
Yeah. Right when we started high school.

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:36.230
Dang, you're huge.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:39.100
Hey! Want to play volleyball with me?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:41.730
Volleyball? You?

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:46.230
I mean, I know I'm small, but I'll grow soon!

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.440
And then, I'm gonna be a super ace like Gaichi!

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.150
A super ace?

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:56.900
The spiker on the team that's the coolest
and the one everyone relies on the most!

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.560
So, come on! Let's play volleyball together!

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:05.060
Truly, I can't thank Oda enough.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:09.020
But, yeah, I don't see myself
playing past college.

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.650
If we lose in the finals two weeks from now,

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:14.270
Oda and I will be retiring then.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:17.350
I'm probably not going to college around here.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:23.400
It's probably normal to only keep in touch
when we come back to town after that.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:26.770
Haijima!

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:28.150
Yes?

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:31.190
Promise me we're gonna make it
to the Spring Tournament.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:34.520
To make that happen,
I'll do whatever you ask us to do.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.400
Right. We'll definitely make it.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.400
You don't even need to think about it.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.190
I've already decided this a while ago.

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:42.270
Well, aren't you dependable?

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:44.980
That's why I'm here.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.810
11/29

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.810
11/29

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.810
Spring Nationals Fukui 
Prefecture Representative Play-offs

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.810
Spring Nationals Fukui 
Prefecture Representative Play-offs

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:54.100
It's November...
It's supposed to be autumn, still.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.310
Kuroba!

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:02.730
You can't ride your bike in this snow.

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:06.190
Hurry up and get ready.
We'll give you a ride to the station.

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.100
You all here, Seiin?

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:16.600
Yes!

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.270
We've been here plenty of times before,

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:22.020
but the snow makes it seem like another world.

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:25.230
What are you talking about?
We're still in our prefecture.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:28.560
Er, yeah... You're right.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.100
This isn't our last stop!

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.520
We're gonna take down Fukuho and head to Tokyo!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.520
We may be the dark horse team
with only eight measly players,

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.480
and the champions and their wall
are going to stand in our way.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:42.480
At least, that's what the
local newspaper said about us.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:44.690
Let's go break through the champions' wall!

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:45.810
Yeah!

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.100
Die!

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.600
Whoa, there.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.020
Nice kill, Kohei!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:57.520
What the heck are they doing?

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:01.060
Subaru Mimura...

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:03.940
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.440
Not a worry in the world.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:07.600
Let's go.

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.480
Okay, that's enough!

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.150
Stop already!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.940
Guys, seriously...

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:40.600
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:47.810
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:56.650
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:00.690
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:13.020
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:19.980
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:26.150
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:32.600
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:40.060
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:47.190
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:56.100
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:56.100 --> 00:22:04.310
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:13.810
It's been so long since I've played
in the center court of a huge venue.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:16.310
The team representing Fukui
will be decided here.

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:17.560
I can't wait...

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:18.900
Until we win.

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.690
Dude, your face!

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:26.940
You look like some girl at a cake buffet
that's determined to eat every kind!

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:31.150
Is that... an ambulance?

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:35.940
We're all here... and there's no audience yet.

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:37.100
Does that mean...

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:38.400
Fukuho?

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:49.440
It looks like someone from Fukuho did get hurt.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:54.020
It's not Mimura.

00:22:57.400 --> 00:22:59.480
Then who...
